# Template for client/ToBe/.env
#
# You almost certainly do NOT need this file. Both local development and the
# Vercel deployment work with no .env at all — see src/apiConfig.js, which
# defaults to http://localhost:5000 in dev and to relative paths in a build.
#
# WARNING: everything here ships to the browser. Vite inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed variable into the built JavaScript, so anything placed in
# this file is publicly readable by anyone who loads the site. Never put a
# secret here — API keys and passwords belong in server/.env, which is never
# sent to the client.

# Overrides where the client sends API requests. Leave it unset unless you
# have a specific reason.
#
# How the deployment actually works, and why this stays empty in production:
#
#   Browser -> tobe-kk.vercel.app/api/events
#                 (Vercel rewrites it server-side, see vercel.json)
#              -> tobe-kk.onrender.com/api/events
#
# The browser only ever talks to the Vercel domain. That is deliberate and
# load-bearing: the session cookie is SameSite=Lax, so if the client called
# onrender.com directly, every API request would be cross-site, the browser
# would refuse to send the cookie, and admin login would stop working — while
# every public page kept loading normally, which makes it painful to diagnose.
#
# So: do NOT set this to the Render URL. If you point it at onrender.com you
# will break admin login. The routing lives in vercel.json instead.
#
# Read at BUILD time, not runtime — changing it requires a rebuild.
# A trailing slash is stripped automatically (see src/apiConfig.js).
VITE_API_URL=
